# mm.shell.posix

Host-only POSIX shell and process environment services: current_shell reads
$SHELL, get/set/unset wrap POSIX getenv/setenv/unsetenv against this process's
real environment, and parse_script classifies a script's physical lines.

HostServices supplies the concrete host providers for the abstract file, I/O,
process, and signal services mm.shell.full declares. Every POSIX header is
confined to a private source unit and no POSIX type crosses an exported
declaration: a handle is an index into HostServices' own tables. Child setup
reports a pre-exec failure through a dedicated close-on-exec pipe, so a missing
program, an unexecutable one, and an infrastructure fault stay distinct.

buildable-target no because setenv, unsetenv, fork, and host process
inspection are POSIX-specific and newlib does not provide them for freestanding
targets.
